{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "kind": "r_hand_derived_ground_truth",
  "derivation": "Each fact below was written by reading the R source of the fixture and applying the documented R analyzer contract. No fact was copied from analyzer output. Line numbers are 1-based and count the fixture's own lines.",
  "fixtures": "bb_tests/fixtures",
  "notes": [
    "R has no block scope, so a name assigned inside a top-level for/while/repeat/if body IS a global binding in R; the analyzer emits it and this is not counted a false positive.",
    "A function defined inside another function is an execution local, not a file-level declaration, and is not a symbol.",
    "A `name -> value` and `value -> name` both bind `name`; `->>` is the superassignment form and binds the same way.",
    "`::` and `:::` both name a package; the RHS field carries the bare function name in both cases.",
    "R06-member-range: a member is written `name = value`, and the symbol's range must span the DECLARATION, starting at the name. R's own lexer puts `size` at 4:5 and `token` at 16:5 in F03-r6.R, so the previous expectation (4:12-4:14, 16:13-16:18) was the VALUE alone and did not contain the name the symbol is published under. The R-positions oracle found 833 such members across the pinned corpora, every one an R6 or R5 method. The expectation was corrected to match R, not the analyzer.",
    "F16-runtime-semantics: every symbol here was taken from R EXECUTING the file, not from reading the analyzer. Found by a red-team cross-check that evaluated each corpus file and asked R's environment what it held; it disagreed with the R-oracle on 8 files, and the R-oracle disagreed with the analyzer's own blind spots in the SAME direction, so the differential's 1.000000 was agreement rather than verification. Three classes: a QUOTED assignment target (`\"%+replace%\" <- ...`, which ggplot2 writes at theme-current.R:130) published nothing; a statically dead `if (FALSE)` branch published declarations R never makes; a top-level `rm()` left the removed helper published. R binds 8 names and excludes dead_one, dead_two, dead_three, removed_helper and inside_fn."
  ],
